{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"theocratic-actuarial-ibex","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\n`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_unrelated_remote_rejection_merges_and_rebuilds_private_candidate`\nfailed once in a full `make verify` run on macOS (Python 3.12.13, `PYTEST_WORKERS=4`, worker\n`gw0`), and PASSES on its own (73 s, 1 passed) on the SAME tree immediately afterwards. So it\nis order- or concurrency-sensitive, not a deterministic break.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\ntests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:41: in _run_git\n    proc = subprocess.run([\"git\", *argv], check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\nE   subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['git', '-C', '<tmp>/test_unrelated_remote_rejectio0',\n    'clone', '--quiet', '-b', 'tickets',\n    '<tmp>/test_unrelated_remote_rejectio0/tickets-remote.git',\n    '<tmp>/test_unrelated_remote_rejectio0/remote-writer']' returned non-zero exit status 128\n```\n\nThe failing call is the test's own `_git(tmp_path, \"clone\", \"--quiet\", \"-b\", \"tickets\", …)` at\n`test_atomic_completion_close.py:47`. `--quiet` means git's own diagnosis was DISCARDED, so the\n128 has no cause attached — that is the first thing to fix, independently of the root cause.\n\n## Why this needs a root cause, not a retry\n\n`AGENTS.md`: a flaky test is a BUG to root-cause, never a retry. It is a regression oracle for\nthe atomic-completion close path; an intermittently red one erodes that. Exit 128 from\n`clone -b <branch>` is most often \"Remote branch tickets not found in upstream origin\" — i.e. a\nrace in which the `tickets` branch is not yet present in the bare remote when the clone runs.\nUnder `-n 4 --dist worksteal` several lifecycle tests drive real git against per-test temp\nremotes, so the hypothesis to test first is that the fixture creates the bare remote and pushes\n`tickets` without a barrier the clone waits on. That is a hypothesis, NOT a finding: reproduce\nit deterministically (`/rebar-debug`) before changing anything.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `128` has a diagnosis: `_run_git` surfaces git's stderr on failure (drop `--quiet` on\n      this call, or include `proc.stderr` in the raised message), so the next occurrence names\n      its own cause instead of an exit code.\n- [ ] The failure is reproduced deterministically (a loop or a forced ordering under xdist) and\n      the root cause is stated with a citation, before any fix.\n- [ ] The fixed test passes N consecutive full-suite runs at `PYTEST_WORKERS=4` with no\n      recurrence; the fix addresses the CLASS (whatever ordering/barrier assumption is wrong),\n      not this one test.\n\n## Discovery\n\nSeen while verifying story `friendless-alabaster-cub` (`4cfc-2de2-747d-4388`); that change\ntouches only `tests/unit/store/test_windows_exclusive_leg.py` and a `sweep (windows)` workflow\nstep and cannot reach this code path. Unrelated to it — filed so the flake is tracked rather\nthan re-run.","id":"57d2-e356-7eb4-4bf5","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_atomic_completion_close: `git clone -b tickets` of the local tickets remote intermittently exits 128 under xdist"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788609132293756831,"uuid":"e80ccd61-0cc0-4f87-9212-724bd808e3e3"}